<title>TURKEY: Shell, others eye Turkmen gas line-Turkey minister.</title>
<headline>Shell, others eye Turkmen gas line-Turkey minister.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian Eni's Snamprogetti, Gas de France and Shell were interested in forming a consortium to build a 3,200 km, $1.6 billion pipeline to carry 28 to 30 billion cubic metres of gas from Turkmenistan to Europe via Iran and Turkey, Turkish energy minister Recai Kutan said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;Three companies said they were interested to set up a consortium to build a 3,200 km pipeline to carry 28 to 30 billion cubic metres of Turkmen gas to Europe via Iran and Turkey. The cost of the project is $1.6 billion,&quot; Kutan told a news conference.</p>
<p>&quot;Snamprogetti, Gas de France and Shell,&quot; Kutan said when asked for the names of the companies.</p>
</text>
